INSERT INTO faq_guidance_refresh VALUES
('Enrollment','How do I enroll in courses?',E'1. Open Enrollment and choose the enrollment term.\n2. Select the published subjects for your saved program and year level. Review their schedules before submitting.\n3. Click Enroll Now to send your selections for review. This is a pending request, not an approved enrollment.\n4. Return to Enrollment to check the request status. The dean reviews requests and assigns teachers.\nIf there are no subjects, confirm the term, program and year on your profile with the Registrar. Subjects require an open term and a matching curriculum. Billing is on a separate page; there is no Fee Review step.','enroll enrollment courses subjects register selections term program year pending approval'),
('Enrollment','What is the enrollment process step by step?',E'1. Open Enrollment and choose the enrollment term.\n2. Check the subjects you want to request and review their schedules.\n3. Click Enroll Now. Your selections are submitted as pending requests for approval.\n4. Check Enrollment for the review result. The dean approves requests and assigns teachers.\nYou are not enrolled merely because you submitted a request. After approval, review Certificate (COR) for your enrolled subjects. Billing remains separate.','enrollment process steps select submit pending dean approval certificate'),
('Enrollment','Can I drop a course after enrolling?','Unchecking a subject changes only your unsubmitted selection. It does not remove an approved enrollment. Once enrolled, ask the Registrar to review a subject change through a consultation. The portal prevents a second enrollment request for a term in which you are already enrolled. School staff must confirm any applicable academic or financial rules.','drop unenroll withdraw cancel change approved enrolled subject'),
('Enrollment','How many units should I enroll in?','Open Grades & Evaluation and choose View Degree Prospectus to review the curriculum. Enrollment shows the total units of your selected subjects. Ask the dean or Registrar to confirm the permitted load for your situation; this assistant has no verified school-wide minimum, maximum, or overload policy.','units load minimum maximum overload prospectus curriculum'),
('Enrollment','When does enrollment start and end?','Check Enrollment for the term currently open for subject requests and the portal notifications for opening notices. The Registrar manages term opening and closing. Ask the Registrar for official dates or late-enrollment requirements; an open term alone does not establish a deadline or a late fee.','enrollment start end dates deadline open close late'),
('Grades','How do I check my grades?',E'1. Open Grades & Evaluation from the sidebar.\n2. Use the Semester selector to choose the term you want to review. Use Year level to narrow the subjects if needed.\n3. Read the subject rows for Pre-lim, Midterm, Semi-finals, Finals, Equivalent and Remark. Grade Estimate is an estimate, not an official result.\n4. Choose View Degree Prospectus to see your curriculum and recorded completion.\nIf a grade is missing or looks wrong, check the selected term first. Book a consultation for staff to review your record; the assistant cannot see your personal grades or confirm their release status.','check see view grades results semester year missing blank midterm final'),
('Grades','When are grades released?','Open Grades & Evaluation and select the relevant semester to see the grades currently available in the portal. Release timing must be confirmed by the school; this guide does not establish a fixed number of days after exams. If you expected a grade and it is missing, first check the selected term, then book a consultation for staff to review the record.','grades release available missing midterm final results'),
('Grades','What is the AI Grade Prediction?','The portal displays Grade Estimate and Estimated GWA. These are calculations from available school grades, not a trained AI prediction or an official final result. The subject estimate uses the available grading periods with equal weight; Estimated GWA weights eligible subject estimates by units. Conditional grades and legacy percentage records are excluded.','ai grade prediction estimate estimated gwa available periods'),
('Grades','How is the GWA computed?','The portal computes a unit-weighted average of eligible recorded school grades: multiply each included subject grade by its units, add those values, then divide by the included units. Grades & Evaluation also shows an estimated GWA based on available grading periods. An estimate is not an official result. This article does not establish eligibility for honors or a Dean''s List cutoff.','gwa average weighted units computation estimate honor'),
('Grades','What is a passing grade?','The portal''s school grade scale labels 3.0 as the minimum passing grade, 4.0 as Conditional / INC, and 5.0 as Failed. Review the Equivalent and Remark columns in Grades & Evaluation. Ask school staff to confirm the process and deadline for resolving an incomplete grade; this guide does not establish an automatic one-year deadline.','passing grade scale conditional inc incomplete failed equivalent remark'),
('General','How do I get my Certificate of Registration?',E'1. Open Certificate (COR) from the sidebar, or choose View & Print COR from the user menu.\n2. Review the student details, term and enrolled subject list. The COR uses your current semester and enrolled subjects, not pending selections.\n3. Click Print Certificate to open the browser print dialog. If your browser offers Save as PDF, you can use that destination.\nIf the subjects or term are missing or incorrect, ask the Registrar to check the enrollment record through a consultation. The assistant cannot issue or certify a COR.','certificate registration cor print pdf enrolled subjects current semester'),
('General','How do I view my class schedule?',E'1. Open Class Schedule from the sidebar.\n2. Review the displayed enrolled subjects and their published meeting days, times, rooms and instructors. Times use Manila time.\nIf a subject has no published meeting time, ask the Registrar to confirm it. A pending subject request or a missing schedule is not proof of a confirmed class time.','schedule timetable class day time room instructor view'),
('Clearance','What is online clearance?',E'1. Open Online Clearance from the sidebar.\n2. Review each office''s status and any note on its clearance card.\n3. Follow the instructions from an office marked Action Required.\n4. Check again after that office reviews the requirement. Only authorized school staff approve clearances.\nPending means the requirement has not been cleared; this assistant cannot clear it or determine your personal eligibility.','online clearance view status process pending action required office'),
('Clearance','What departments need to clear me?','Open Online Clearance to see the offices on your actual clearance record. The portal supports Registrar, Cashier, Guidance, Dean, DSA, Laboratory/Nursing Arts/Cybershack, Library, Medical/Dental Clinic, Property Custodian and ROTC/CWTS. Read each office''s status and note. Follow the offices listed for your account rather than assuming a general list establishes your eligibility.','clearance departments offices registrar cashier guidance dean library dsa laboratory medical property rotc'),
('Clearance','Why is my clearance showing Action Required?','Action Required means an office needs an action before it can clear that requirement. Open Online Clearance and read that office''s note for the actual instruction. If the note is unclear or the status looks wrong, book a consultation so staff can review it. The assistant cannot determine the reason from your private clearance record.','action required clearance hold block note pending'),
('Clearance','How do I get cleared by the library?','Open Online Clearance and check the Library card and note. Follow the Library''s instructions about any outstanding borrowed items or obligations, then allow authorized Library staff to review the requirement. Ask the Library to confirm specific fines or conditions; the assistant cannot inspect your borrowing record or approve clearance.','library clearance books return borrowed fine note'),
('Billing','How do I pay my tuition?',E'1. Open Billing & History.\n2. Review the assessed balance, any published installment schedule and transaction history.\n3. Follow the payment instructions issued by the Cashier''s Office. Payments are recorded by Cashier staff; the portal has no online payment button.\nIf a payment is missing or the balance looks wrong, book a consultation for staff to review the record. The assistant cannot see your balance or verify a payment.','pay payment tuition billing balance history transaction cashier'),
('Billing','Can I pay in installments?','Open Billing & History and check whether the Cashier has published an installment schedule for your term. If one is shown, review its amounts and dates. If none is shown, ask the Cashier to confirm the available arrangement; an empty schedule does not establish that the entire balance is immediately due. Payments and payment status are recorded by Cashier staff.','installment payment plan partial schedule terms cashier'),
('Billing','How much is the tuition per unit?','Use Billing & History to review the assessment recorded for your account. Ask the Cashier''s Office for the official current fee schedule and an explanation of specific charges. This assistant has no verified per-unit tuition rates and must not estimate amounts.','tuition per unit cost price fee assessment amount'),
('Billing','What payment methods are accepted?','Ask the Cashier''s Office for the currently accepted payment channels and their instructions. This guide does not confirm a bank, wallet or online payment method. Billing & History displays the assessment and payment transactions recorded by Cashier staff; it does not accept payments.','payment method cash bank online cashier transaction'),
('General','Can I access the LMS and Career Hub from this portal?','Use Quick Links in the sidebar to open the configured LMS or Career Hub link when available for your role. The destination may require its own sign-in. A link does not guarantee automatic single sign-on, and this assistant cannot confirm the destination''s account state.','lms career hub quick links access sso sign in'),
('General','How do I contact support?','For a question that needs staff review, use Book a consultation in the portal help area. Choose the topic, enter the details and submit the request. A request is not a confirmed appointment; check its status for staff confirmation. For a login problem that prevents portal access, use the school''s official support channel. This guide does not publish verified support email addresses.','support help consultation contact appointment login technical'),
('General','How do I reset my 2FA / authenticator?','If you cannot access your authenticator, use the recovery options actually shown on the sign-in page and follow the school''s account-recovery instructions. If you cannot complete verification, contact the school through an official support channel. Do not assume that signing in again or scanning a new QR code bypasses an existing MFA requirement.','2fa mfa reset authenticator lost phone recovery qr'),
('General','How do I set up Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)?','Follow the authenticator setup shown during sign-in or open the authenticator settings available in your user menu. Scan the QR code with your authenticator app and enter its current six-digit code to verify. Never share the setup secret or verification codes. If setup fails, use the school''s account-support process.','2fa mfa setup authenticator totp qr code'),
('General','What email do I use to log in?','Sign in with the official institutional email account issued to you by IMCC. Complete the requested profile details, including program and year level for student requests. Account approval and role assignment are managed by the school; an email pattern alone does not establish that access has been approved.','email login sign in institutional school account approval'),
('General','What email domains are allowed?','Use the institutional email account issued by the school, such as an authorized @imcc.edu.ph account. The sign-in configuration determines which institutional domains are accepted. Do not choose a different domain to obtain a role; your portal role and approval come from the school-managed account profile.','email domain institutional allowed school account role');
